@id n4_simon
# DRAFT
# Brother Simon at dusk, in the cloister garth on the low wall of the herb beds (night 4, fog). A quiet choir brother; nervous.
# Not in the cult. Thomas has sent him to do a dirty job tonight (scrubbing blood) and he can't say so.
# If Thomas has named him (n4_thomas_simon), the porter can ask where he goes at night (trust -5: he takes it badly).
# Telling him to keep to the dormitory is a warning ([warn]); he takes it badly, and he trusts Thomas more than the porter.
# Claims: n4_simon_night (hiding): he can't sleep, he walks. True, but Thomas sends him out at night; pressed, he says he's bid, not by whom.
== start
(A thin brother on the wall of the herb beds, picking at a thread on his sleeve. He stands too fast when he sees you.)
Simon {ashamed, look down}: Porter. I was only taking the air. There's not much else to take tonight.
-> topics

== again
(Simon is back on the wall, picking at the same thread.)
Simon {ashamed}: Porter.
-> topics

== topics
* [if n4_thomas_simon] [if not n4_simon_night] Where do you go at night, brother? -> night
* [if not n4_simon_how] How are you keeping, brother? -> how
* [if not n4_simon_warn] Keep to the dormitory tonight, brother. Bar the door. [warn] -> warn

== night [set n4_simon_night] [trust simon -5] [claim n4_simon_night hiding]
(The thread snaps in his fingers.)
Simon {afraid}: Who says I go anywhere? I can't sleep. I walk. Is that a sin now, with all the rest?
* [believe] No sin, brother. I can't sleep either. -> night_believed
* [press] Walk where, brother? Alone, at that hour? -> night_pressed

== night_believed
(He looks toward the infirmary, then at the ground.)
Simon {ashamed, look down}: No. No sin. Leave me be, porter.
-> topics

== night_pressed
(He looks toward the infirmary, then at the ground.)
Simon {ashamed, swallow}: I go where I'm bid, porter. I do what I'm told, and I don't ask. I'm not to talk of it.
Simon {pleading, look down}: Don't ask me again. Please.
-> topics

== how [set n4_simon_how]
Simon {ashamed}: Hungry. Cold. Afraid, like everyone.
Simon {sad, look down}: I came here to sing, porter. It's all I'm good for. I wish they'd let me only sing.
-> topics

== warn [set n4_simon_warn]
(He goes white.)
Simon {afraid, look down}: Why would you say that to me? Who told you to say it?
Simon {ashamed}: I'll go where I'm bid. I'm a brother of this house, not a guest you can lock in.
Simon {pleading, look down}: Don't tell anyone you said that to me. Please.
-> end

== leave
Simon {ashamed}: God keep you, porter.
